            <circle class="dot" cx="750" cy="183" r="4" fill="var(--rose)"/>
            <circle class="dot" cx="750" cy="46" r="4" fill="var(--gold)"/>
            <circle class="dot" cx="750" cy="22" r="4" fill="var(--teal)"/>
          </svg>
          <div class="chartcard-foot">
            <span>t0 — dollar turns</span>
            <span>t+n — gold confirms</span>
            <span>t+2n — bitcoin follows</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="thesis">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="kicker">The thesis</div>
        <h2>One market, three tickers</h2>
        <p class="section-lede">Most trading content treats DXY, Gold, and Bitcoin as unrelated stories. The macro read here is that they're one liquidity story on staggered clocks — and reading the lead-lag correctly is the actual edge.</p>
        <div class="thesis-grid">
          <div class="thesis-cell">
            <div class="thesis-num mono">01</div>
            <h4>Dollar turns first</h4>
            <p>DXY reacts fastest to rate expectations and liquidity shifts — it's the leading indicator, not the lagging headline.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="thesis-cell">
            <div class="thesis-num mono">02</div>
            <h4>Gold confirms</h4>
            <p>Gold repositions as a hard-money hedge once the dollar move is established — the confirmation leg.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="thesis-cell">
            <div class="thesis-num mono">03</div>
            <h4>Bitcoin follows</h4>
            <p>Bitcoin picks up the liquidity trade last, often the most exaggerated of the three moves.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="pillars">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="kicker">What you'll get</div>
        <h2>Two formats, one standard: show your work</h2>
        <p class="section-lede">Every video either explains the macro read or proves it with a real trade. No unverified calls, no signal selling.</p>
        <div class="pillars">
          <div class="pillar">
            <span class="tag">Weekly</span>
            <h4>Macro Read</h4>
            <p>DXY / Gold / BTC intermarket analysis — what's actually driving price, and what it implies next across all three.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="pillar">
            <span class="tag">Weekly</span>
            <h4>Trade Log</h4>
            <p>Screen-recorded, real trades from a verified account — entry logic, invalidation, and the outcome, wins and losses alike.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="pillar wide">
            <span class="tag">Standing rule</span>
            <h4>If it's on screen, it's real</h4>
            <p>Every P&L, order ticket, and chart shown is genuinely screen-recorded from a live account. That's the entire premise of this channel — if you can't verify it, it doesn't go in the video.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="credentials">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="kicker">Track record</div>
        <h2>The receipts live on the main portfolio</h2>
        <div class="cred">
          <div class="cred-copy">
            <p>Trading credentials, prop-firm status, and platform details are kept on the full IT × Markets portfolio and updated manually — never synced live, so account credentials stay off any public site.</p>
            <a href="https://shariefvp.github.io/myportfolio/#markets" class="linkout">See the full markets profile ↗</a>
          </div>
          <div class="cred-stats">
            <div class="cred-stat"><div class="n mono">FTMO</div><div class="l">Prop firm</div></div>
            <div class="cred-stat"><div class="n mono">MT5</div><div class="l">Execution platform</div></div>
            <div class="cred-stat"><div class="n mono">DXY</div><div class="l">Primary lead indicator</div></div>
            <div class="cred-stat"><div class="n mono">XAU · BTC</div><div class="l">Confirmation legs</div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="notify" class="notify">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="kicker">Launch list</div>
        <h2>Be first to watch when it goes live</h2>
        <div class="notify-panel">
          <div>
            <h3>No spam. One email at launch.</h3>
            <p>You'll hear from me once — when the first Macro Read and Trade Log videos are up.</p>
          </div>
          <form class="notify-form" id="notifyForm">
            <label for="email" class="sr-only" style="position:absolute; left:-9999px;">Email address</label>
            <input id="email" type="email" name="email" placeholder="you@email.com" required>
            <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary" style="border:none; cursor:pointer;" id="notifyBtn">Notify me</button>
          </form>
          <p class="form-note" id="notifyStatus" style="margin-top:12px;"></p>
        </div>
        <p class="form-note">Submissions are sent to a Google Sheet — see APPS_SCRIPT_SETUP.md for the 5-minute setup.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="foot-row">
        <span>© 2026 Sharief Pacasirang — The Macro Signal</span>
        <a href="https://shariefvp.github.io/myportfolio/">← Back to full portfolio</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <script>
    // ---- Notify form → Google Sheet via Apps Script Web App ----
    // Replace this with your deployed Web App URL (see APPS_SCRIPT_SETUP.md).
    var SCRIPT_URL = "https://script.google.com/macros/s/AKfycbxoVhWdeQaLI6G57POV8IuNWfd967URMk_wTHYA6w4G8fy5HOcgQDrlV91ZRUmspj41Pg/exec";

    var form = document.getElementById('notifyForm');
    var status = document.getElementById('notifyStatus');
    var btn = document.getElementById('notifyBtn');

    form.addEventListener('submit', function (e) {
      e.preventDefault();

      if (SCRIPT_URL.indexOf('PASTE_YOUR') === 0) {
        status.textContent = 'Form not connected yet — add your Apps Script URL in the code.';
        return;
      }

      var email = document.getElementById('email').value.trim();
      if (!email) return;

      btn.disabled = true;
      btn.textContent = 'Sending…';
      status.textContent = '';

      fetch(SCRIPT_URL, {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'text/plain;charset=utf-8' }, // avoids CORS preflight
        body: JSON.stringify({
          email: email,
          source: 'macro-signal-landing',
          page: window.location.href,
          submittedAt: new Date().toISOString()
        })
      })
        .then(function (res) { return res.json(); })
        .then(function (data) {
          if (data && data.result === 'success') {
            form.reset();
            status.textContent = "You're on the list — see you at launch.";
          } else {
            status.textContent = 'Something went wrong. Please try again.';
          }
        })
        .catch(function () {
          status.textContent = 'Something went wrong. Please try again.';
        })
        .finally(function () {
          btn.disabled = false;
          btn.textContent = 'Notify me';
        });
    });
  </script>

